-- Measures known-size construction followed by a known-size transform.
use sequence as items.
use testing as check.

function double(value unsigned 64) giving unsigned 64 {
  give value multiply 2.
}

dynamic values is items.sized[unsigned 64](10_000) try.
dynamic index of type unsigned 64 is 0.
while index less than 10_000 {
  set values at index to index.
  increase index by 1.
}

constant doubled is items.map[unsigned 64, unsigned 64](values, double) try.
after {
  items.release[unsigned 64](values) fallback nothing.
  items.release[unsigned 64](doubled) fallback nothing.
}

check.number(items.length[unsigned 64](doubled), 10_000).
check.number(doubled at 9_999, 19_998).
